WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.389
So a good Just Cause

00:00:08.389 --> 00:00:10.490
is not for any

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:13.350
particular group of people.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:15.190
It is idealized

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:16.190
in the sense that anyone who

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:17.190
believes in that vision of the

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:19.310
future is invited to join.

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:21.010
So if you believe all

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:22.420
people are created equal and that's

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:23.599
the world you want to live in, join

00:00:23.599 --> 00:00:25.220
the Cause.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:27.130
If you believe my Just Cause it's,

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:28.689
I imagine, a world in which the vast

00:00:28.689 --> 00:00:30.570
majority of people wake up

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:32.630
every single morning inspired,

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:35.030
feel safe wherever they are,

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:36.030
and end the day fulfilled by the

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:37.310
work that they do.

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:38.640
If that appeals to you, then join

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:39.680
our Cause.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.430
And it doesn't, it doesn't

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:42.980
leave anyone out.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:44.070
So that's, so it has to be

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:45.070
inclusive.

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:46.070
It has to be stated in a

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:47.230
way that anyone who wants to build

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.190
that world could build that world.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:50.760
A Just Cause must be for

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:52.329
others, not for yourself.

00:00:52.329 --> 00:00:53.379
There's no such thing as a Just

00:00:53.379 --> 00:00:56.620
Cause for me, right?

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:58.010
The world that you hope to benefit,

00:00:58.010 --> 00:00:59.710
the company, the world that you hope

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:00.859
to build, the company you hope to

00:01:00.859 --> 00:01:02.660
build, the family you hope to build

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:04.230
is for others, it's so that others

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.570
may enjoy it.

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:08.080
And I think this mistake is made a

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:09.350
lot, especially when companies

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:10.550
articulate their visions.

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:12.490
It's about them.

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:13.490
To be

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:14.490
the best, to be the most respected,

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:16.030
to be the, you know, whatever it is.

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:17.710
That that benefits no one else

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:18.770
but you.

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:19.770
And

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:21.550
a Just Cause must be to the benefit

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:23.000
of others.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Idealistic is the easy

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.270
one, which is stated in

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:27.020
terms that are literally

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.479
unachievable.

00:01:29.479 --> 00:01:31.170
So idealistic is the fun one.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:32.350
If you make it achievable, well,

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:33.350
then it's just a goal and it's a

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:35.130
milestone and it's not truly

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:36.579
a Just Cause.

00:01:36.579 --> 00:01:38.840
So yeah, idealism is essential.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.790
So resilient is different than

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:43.141
stable, because stable

00:01:43.141 --> 00:01:45.220
is like if a ship

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:47.130
is stable, you know it goes into the

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:49.100
storm and it comes out of the storm.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:50.420
And it survived the storm.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:53.590
But it's still the same ship, right?

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:55.329
Stable companies survive things,

00:01:55.329 --> 00:01:56.880
but they're still the same companies.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.350
Resilience is the ability to adapt

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:00.579
and change and a resilient

00:02:00.579 --> 00:02:02.659
organization, a resilient family.

00:02:02.659 --> 00:02:04.219
A resilient family goes into

00:02:04.219 --> 00:02:06.280
tragedy, the loss of a loved one,

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.320
you know, the sudden loss of a loved

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:10.090
one and they come out

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:11.540
different.

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:13.410
They come through that stronger

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:14.910
people.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:15.910
Resilient organizations have

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:17.349
gone into the pandemic

00:02:17.349 --> 00:02:20.379
and their

00:02:20.379 --> 00:02:21.980
cultures are different.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:24.170
They've adapted,

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:26.819
they're stronger, their

00:02:26.819 --> 00:02:30.379
relationships are more intense.

00:02:30.379 --> 00:02:32.060
And so resilience is the ability to

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:34.360
adapt and

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:36.280
grow and strengthen, not just

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:39.090
be so filled with concrete

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:40.090
that you just make it through

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:43.760
something.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:48.550
Well, Just Causes is

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:49.849
about idealism.

00:02:49.849 --> 00:02:51.331
It's about imagining a future, a

00:02:51.331 --> 00:02:53.530
future that doesn't exist

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:54.530
right now.

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:55.810
So in the United States, we have a

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:58.230
declaration of independence in which

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:00.019
the founding fathers have said they

00:03:00.019 --> 00:03:01.610
imagine a world in which all men are

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:02.610
created equal.

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:04.550
All people are equal,

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:05.959
endowed with unalienable rights,

00:03:05.959 --> 00:03:06.970
amongst which include life, liberty

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:08.200
and the pursuit of happiness.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:09.870
Now we're clearly not there,

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:10.980
but it is a striving.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:12.000
It is a pursuit.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.000
And by the way,

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.569
we'll never get there, but we'll die

00:03:14.569 --> 00:03:15.569
trying.

00:03:15.569 --> 00:03:17.200
Or Martin Luther King, who imagined

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:18.650
a world very different to the one he

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:19.650
grew up in.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:20.650
We're still not there

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:22.640
and but we'll die trying.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.430
And the milestones that we pass,

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:27.060
whether it's legislative or

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:28.270
civil rights or gay rights or

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:30.450
women's suffrage, you know, these

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:32.239
are stepping stones that

00:03:32.239 --> 00:03:33.560
prove to us that we're moving in the

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.500
right direction and

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:37.780
having a Just Cause a sense of a

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:39.010
future state that we're working

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:41.129
towards is what gives our lives

00:03:41.129 --> 00:03:42.459
and our work meaning.

00:03:42.459 --> 00:03:45.330
It's, I think, important to

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:47.610
note that the women's

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:48.610
suffrage movement in the United

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:50.569
States, that every

00:03:50.569 --> 00:03:52.459
single founder, every single

00:03:52.459 --> 00:03:53.960
founder of the women's suffrage move

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:55.790
in the United States died before

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:57.439
the first woman ever voted.

00:03:57.439 --> 00:03:59.959
Now, do you think they felt like

00:03:59.959 --> 00:04:01.590
their lives were failures?

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:03.209
No, of course not.

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:04.209
It's because they could see the

00:04:04.209 --> 00:04:05.209
growing movement.

00:04:05.209 --> 00:04:06.209
They could see the

00:04:06.209 --> 00:04:07.209
momentum, they could see that they

00:04:07.209 --> 00:04:08.209
were moving closer and closer

00:04:08.209 --> 00:04:09.209
towards their vision.

00:04:09.209 --> 00:04:10.209
Would they'd like to have done to

00:04:10.209 --> 00:04:12.760
how to go quicker, of course.

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:13.940
But they could see that others took

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.970
their torch and promised to carry it

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:17.590
for them after they died and their

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.910
Cause was no longer there as it

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:21.350
became the Cause of others.

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:22.950
And to have a sense

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:25.710
of Just Cause means that

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:27.090
it doesn't belong to any one of us,

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:28.440
but it becomes all of ours.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:29.440
And that's what gives us the

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:31.120
confidence and we can all lie on our

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:32.720
deathbeds and say, "I'm passing

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:33.940
something on."

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.770
By the way,

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:37.420
this is a big deal in families.

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:39.770
This is why families have legacies.

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:41.500
And this is why carrying our last

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:43.600
name matters

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:44.600
because there are those who came

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.040
before us and we want to honor those

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:47.040
who came before us.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:48.040
We don't want to

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:49.040
let them down.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:50.590
We don't let their sacrifices

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:51.920
go in vain.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:53.150
And so having a Just Cause and

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:54.430
feeling a part of something bigger

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:56.300
than ourselves is what gives

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:57.700
our lives and our work and all of

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:00.030
these things legacy.

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:02.100
And there's good data to show

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:03.590
that when we have a sense of our

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:05.070
past, it actually makes

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:06.780
us better equipped to make decisions

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:08.440
for the future.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:09.440
It's ironic, you know, you hear

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:11.120
politicians all the time say, "You

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:12.470
know, we're doing this for our

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:13.470
children."

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:14.470
Well, if we invoked

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:15.610
our children every time we made

00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:17.360
decisions, we make a lot better

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.770
decisions than most of us do.

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:21.660
But if you invoke the past,

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:23.480
it actually makes us better because

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:24.820
as I said before, to see ourselves

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:26.390
not at the beginning of a process,

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:28.600
but in the middle of it, and

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:29.610
that we have responsibility to the

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:31.420
past and we have a responsibility

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:33.390
to ensure that we can pass

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:36.350
it on after our passing,

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:40.240
lots of passes in there.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:41.900
It is actually makes us better

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:43.120
equipped to make better long term

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:43.139
decisions.

